Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:25:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a short notice for a display with Dolby Vision
 Low-Latency only

The notification of a Dolby Vision video on a display that offers Dolby Vision
Low-Latency only was three or four sentences long and stayed on the screen for
15 s (in a test through a box between the PC and the TV: "the banner has a
message that is too long, and it lasts a while").

It says what to do now, in one sentence, for the usual time of a notification:

- where the driver of the output can send Low-Latency and it is off: "The
  display takes only Dolby Vision Low-Latency: turn it on in System > Display,
  or turn off the game settings of the TV input.";
- otherwise: "The display takes only Dolby Vision Low-Latency: turn off the
  game settings of the TV input for native Dolby Vision."

Why it happens (a TV input in its game mode, a device between the source and
the TV that offers that form alone, a display with no other form), and what
native output does, are in the log line, which now also tells the case where
Low-Latency is on and native output did not send it from the one where the
driver cannot send it; the Dolby Vision page of the player information gives
its reason as before. In en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx.
